{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781532199,"nonce":"kWomu9FR0j4ptSlc0+a6fkxu7ck=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABFhpd9A","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/278","origin":"github"},"title":"Wire Lake Massabesic datum (lake_datum: 52.3) into the boat chart_datum node","message":"## Problem\nThe BizzyBoat `chart_datum` node runs at Lake Massabesic with **no datum value\nwired**. `bizzyboat.yaml`'s `/**/chart_datum:` block sets only frame names\n(`chart_datum_frame`, `mhhw_frame`, …) — no `lake_datum`, no `datum_config_path`.\nSo `resolve_datum()` falls through to its default and `chart_datum` is **not**\npublished at the lake surface (≈ ellipsoid 0, not 52.3 m).\n\nThe 52.3 m WGS84 ellipsoidal lake surface (RTK-measured, no tide) currently lives\nonly in the sim world config and in notes — not on the real boat.\n\n## Fix\nAdd the fixed-value override to the boat's `chart_datum` block:\n```yaml\n/**/chart_datum:\n  ros__parameters:\n    ...\n    lake_datum: 52.3        # WGS84 ellipsoidal lake surface (RTK; no tide). Wins outright.\n```\n`lake_datum` \"wins outright\" in `resolve_datum()` precedence (param \u003e polygon \u003e\nVDatum), so no lake-outline polygon is required for the always-in-the-lake boat.\n\n**Deliberately NOT setting `lake_datum_mhhw`.** `sea_surface_estimator` uses the\nMHHW frame only as a tide plausibility filter and **skips the filter when the MHHW\nframe is absent** (safe). Setting MHHW = chart datum would make the tidal range 0\nand reject every tide estimate → `map_tide` would stop updating. Leaving MHHW unset\nkeeps `map_tide` exactly as it behaves today. (A real small lake-level range for the\nfilter can be a later refinement.)\n\n## Impact / sequencing\n- **Not a splash blocker.** chart_datum's only live consumer (the tide filter)\n  ignores it while MHHW is absent; `s57_layer` is disabled (#263); the bathy-store\n  importer that needs the datum isn't on the boat. This is correctness groundwork —\n  it becomes load-bearing when the bathymetry costmap layer (#164) consumes\n  `z(map_tide) − seafloor` clearance.\n- The value is the RTK estimate; refining it is a one-line change.\n- Canonical single-source-of-truth (a `massabesic` polygon `DatumEntry` shared with\n  the store importer, per #163) remains the durable follow-up; this scalar is the\n  correct, robust boat-runtime wiring now.\n\n## Acceptance\n- With the boat config, `chart_datum_node` logs \"lake_datum override set:\n  chart_datum 52.300 m\" and publishes the `chart_datum` frame at 52.3 m ellipsoidal.\n- `map_tide` continues to publish (MHHW absent → filter disabled, unchanged).\n- Verifiable in the Massabesic sim (rolker/unh_marine_simulation#67) before live use.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}